-- gate: reject
-- defect: unresolved name `mysteryValue` (not a Sky/stdlib/local binding)
-- oracle: reject [E1001] naming error at canonicalisation
--
-- CLOSED (was known-leniency). `import Sky.Core.Prelude exposing (..)` opens the
-- `Basics` kernel pseudo-module. The resolver used to lack a static enumeration
-- of `Basics`' exports, so it resolved ANY bare unknown name to a lenient
-- `Res::Kernel` ref rather than emit `[E1001]` — a `sky check ≡ sky build`
-- violation (`main = println mysteryValue` passed `sky check` then failed
-- `go build` with `undefined: rt.Basics_mysteryValue`). Fixed by porting the
-- oracle's `staticKernelFunctions` table (Module.hs:1752) into
-- `hir::kernel::KERNEL_FUNCTIONS`: a kernel `exposing (..)` now binds exactly
-- the module's known functions (mirroring `kernelVarsFor` + `addExposed`,
-- Module.hs:700-703), so an unknown bare name falls through `resolve_var` to
-- `Res::Error` + `[E1001] Undefined name`. Matches the Haskell oracle exactly.
module Main exposing (main)

import Sky.Core.Prelude exposing (..)
import Std.Log exposing (println)

main =
    println mysteryValue
